    "success_criteria": {
      "criteria": [
        "An intent with no external verify command configured behaves identically to today (zero diagnostics, zero subprocess calls, no new required fields) -- this feature is opt-in only.",
        "An intent with an external verify command configured has that command actually invoked at the 3_implement->4_verify phase_advance edge, and lane advance refuses the transition (writes nothing to lane-state.json) whenever the command exits non-zero, times out, or fails to spawn at all.",
        "The command that runs is always exactly the argv recorded at the point the operator's configuration was accepted -- never a string built at run time from a separately-mutable file, and never passed through a shell (so no argument can be reinterpreted as shell syntax).",
        "The gate's own diagnostics never assume or depend on any particular external tool's CLI syntax or output format (only the child process's exit status/timeout/spawn-failure is read) -- deterministic-discipline's dd verify --session is the motivating example, not a hardcoded dependency."
      ],
      "recorded_at": "2026-08-29T13:37:34.416Z"
    }
  }
